  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agriculture Finance Support Facility (AFSF) Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The overall objective of the project is to demonstrate to a broad set  of stakeholders, particularly commercial banks, specialized financial  organizations, development finance organizations, and insurance  companies, that it is possible to profitably provide financial  services to smallholder farmers and other low income clientele located  in rural areas.
 
 This GPP is designed to support the replication or scaling-up of  profitable rural finance business models and the generation of  knowledge and learning about these models. It will provide grants to  commercial banks, specialized financial organizations, such as leasing  companies, development finance organizations, financial cooperative  networks, insurance companies, and to a limited extent, asset  registries, credit bureaus, and training organizations.  It will  support activities that seek to increase access to financial services  in rural areas. It will  fund grantee conferences, study tours for  grantee and World Bank Group staff, a quarterly rural finance seminar  series, and publication of rural finance case studies.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
